From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic_load_fw: no busy-wait under the rx pool lock

aicwf_prealloc_rxbuff_alloc() spins for 10 ms with mdelay(10) when fewer
than 10 buffers are left in the pool, after spin_lock_irqsave() on the
pool lock. Its caller, aicwf_usb_submit_rx_urb() in aic8800_fdrv, runs in
the bulk-in completion, so the host controller's bottom half stalls with
interrupts off for each URB. The wait cannot refill the pool:
aicwf_prealloc_rxbuff_free() takes the same lock.

Drop the mdelay(10) and keep the warning. When the pool is empty the
function already returns NULL, and the caller sets rx_urb_sched so the
busrx thread re-arms the URB once it has freed a buffer.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_rx_prealloc.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_rx_prealloc.c
index d29edfd..551dc6d 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_rx_prealloc.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_rx_prealloc.c
@@ -37,7 +37,6 @@ struct rx_buff *aicwf_prealloc_rxbuff_alloc(spinlock_t *lock)
         AICWFDBG(LOGERROR, "%s WARNING rxbuff is running out %d\r\n", __func__,
             rx_buff_list_ava);
         //msleep(10);
-        mdelay(10);
     }
 
     if (list_empty(&aic_rx_buff_list.rxbuff_list)) {
